User question: 'What are some signs that a habit is becoming addictive and/or negative?'
AI response: 'Officially, there is no such diagnosis as “sugar addiction”.  However, there are some similarities in the symptoms and behaviors associated with addictions to substances like sugar and drugs and alcohol.  Addiction to substances like sugar can lead to similar patterns of behavior and other problems, including:

- excessive use;
- continued use despite problems with work, school, social life, finances; 
- continued use despite problems with physical or mental health; 
- increased tolerance (more is needed to achieve the same effect or produce the same feelings of satisfaction);
- increasing efforts to cut down or control use;
- continuing to abuse the substance despite serious consequences. 

Abuse of any substance can be dangerous and unhealthy.  It is important to seek help from a professional healthcare provider to address any substance abuse or addiction issues.  People with these issues also need support and help from loved ones and family and friends in their support networks.'
Domain: general

User question: 'Using JavaScript, how do I write the code that captures the entered text on an input box and sets it as the value of a variable "email"?'
AI response: 'This code would provide a simple form with an input box that receives your answer, and a simple OK button:      

<form method="post" action="">
Answer: <input type="text" id="input" name="input" submitted>
<input type="submit" value="Submit">
</form>

First we must write an HTML page, with this source code.  HTML is a basic markup language for displaying web pages.

Then we create a simple JavaScript script to tie these elements together.  Here is the code, after we have created a basic HTML page with the input box and button above:

$(document).ready(function(){
$("#input").click(function(){
  var input = document.getElementById("input").value;
  $("#message").html(input);
});
});

We work in JavaScript to create a page that loads automatically on your browser, in response to the user clicking the "Submit" button.  Then we create a basic variable to store the text that the user enters in the form, and an element to display the variable which we call the "message".  Finally we reference this variable in our JavaScript function and display the value inside the "message" element.  Let me know if you have any questions about this code!'
